From 9fe8dfa5b7a48ce34cf60156ece2dedd17585b7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:16:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] build: revert the v2.3.2 RuntimeProxy ABI check, which
 does not compile

Revert c54e491a1ea0 ("Add ABI version checking for LiteRtRuntimeCApiStruct
in RuntimeProxy"), the one source change v2.3.2 adds over v2.3.1 apart from
a Kotlin JNI fix. Its litert/cc/internal/litert_runtime_proxy.h calls
LiteRtRuntimeCApiStruct members and uses types (delegation metrics,
litert_create_tensor_buffer_from_custom_handle) that only exist on main
after 0dedf30fc, so every C++ file that includes litert_options.h fails
with GCC 13:

  litert_runtime_proxy.h:674:7: error: LiteRtDelegationMetricsConst has
  not been declared

The ABI check only matters when a system (Google Play services) runtime is
loaded; a static CPU build always uses the builtin runtime.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
